{"title":"1993 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1993 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b3c9a4087f0d3e79d1b138808ecf7695cdff09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^n+5x^{n-1}+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> cannot be expressed as the product of two nonconstant polynomials with integer coefficients.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point inside acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21c114f0fb35ff2c15ca7812e3b36faf9539970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB=\\angle ACB+\\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96dad4ee92208ad7b907068e9bea17203738ef7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cdot BD=AD\\cdot BC$\" width=\"166\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(a) Compute the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032778ba4d2466f8ea9443555dec3ddc3d7df825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AB\\cdot CD)/(AC\\cdot BD).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) Prove that the tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> are perpendicular.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>On an infinite chessboard, a game is played as follows. At the start, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> pieces are arranged on the chessboard in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> block of adjoining squares, one piece in each square. A move in the game is a jump in a horizontal or vertical direction over an adjacent occupied square to an unoccupied square immediately beyond. The piece which has been jumped over is removed. Find those values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which the game can end with only one piece remaining on the board.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For three points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3efd92d7eef6e4b04b61b6ff7e353462a2607585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q,R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> in the plane, we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123b99af69441aa32669471fec916b7cb9aa927b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(PQR)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> as the minimum length of the three altitudes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. (If the points are collinear, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa4ab6298ad04d6dc3add29695a066614cd9c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(PQR)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />.)\n</p><p>Prove that for points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b8268aad986b4baa4939636bcad1483519aa8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> in the plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6c9fa66d5e1f9316b8e10886e20a25f3ce5f27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m(ABC)\\le m(ABX)+m(AXC)+m(XBC).\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Does there exist a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbfbc6de6fa1242cf3769715687e2b74d04cb740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\textbf{N}\\rightarrow\\textbf{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319044b48af4f1596e06734dad4f2026f44d810d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=2,f(f(n))=f(n)+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d668d01df02822c003106eeb35f7f10471d91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\textbf{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fc87c0375162447b03a08afa8d31ab6511f9449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)&lt;f(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d668d01df02822c003106eeb35f7f10471d91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\textbf{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> lamps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca4941f607e8bd64c2a80ac746a4599e894f82b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_0, \\ldots , L_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> in a circle (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />), where we denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56dd375a5a6be7daffa1727a7ac2be5750a02bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{n+k} = L_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. (A lamp at all times is either on or off.) Perform steps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd2d0880ea8b06040a7e9ff65fd01d363e35cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_0, s_1, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> as follows: at step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b63c17213f84d730e0de1f8c08597f7a648e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8880155d396f4a3d93baa809801797acab56b53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> is lit, switch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df66d9f3deecddce3e90ce33836dd65e605ed7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> from on to off or vice versa, otherwise do nothing. Initially all lamps are on. Show that:\n</p><p><br />\n(a) There is a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/eced0857922bc8edbd02bda332578504eb0aaf5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> such that after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/eced0857922bc8edbd02bda332578504eb0aaf5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> steps all the lamps are on again;\n</p><p>(b) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776939957eb5972a7febd68b21f0788c99943f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^k$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f2c523e2747c69f2a48d7479afc3a01233eebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(n) = n^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" />;\n</p><p>(c) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe3b8f0a7df9fd13b4256bc94ac69be9f4595b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />, we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244ebab97bf122926fa86356faadc482e8230f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(n) = n^2 - n + 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO\" title=\"1993 IMO\">1993 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO\" title=\"1992 IMO\">1992 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 255/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7143/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.596      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.596      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17430:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043715 and revision id 221680. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}